    {
      "id": "kpk1-l18-b1-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l18-b1-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Gdzie? W banku, w szkole"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "After *w* (in) and *na* (on, at), asked *gdzie?* (where?), a word takes the locative, *miejscownik*. Most he and it words end in *-e*: *teatr*, *w teatrze*; *sklep*, *w sklepie*; *kino*, *w kinie*. After *k*, *g*, *ch* and soft sounds they end in *-u*: *w banku*, *w hotelu*, *w mieszkaniu*. She words end in *-e* (*w szkole*, *w firmie*), or *-i* and *-y* after soft sounds: *w kawiarni*, *na ulicy*. *Centrum* does not change: *w centrum*."
      },
      "table": {
